From 03babededf0fd472707eb6706bf7259f66c1dffb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Larry Klosowski <larryklosowski@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 16:16:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(tier,fleet): take the hardware read and tier rule from
 citrate-sizeup (F-10)

LOCAL ONLY, NOT PUSHED: depends on citrate-sizeup through a sibling path,
because CitrateNetwork/citrate-sizeup does not exist yet. Exported as
.agentile/sprints/active/sprint-hup-s8-fleet/n7-sizeup-library.patch on
hup/n7-sizeup-library.

tier::probe reads a sizeup receipt (library::probe) and recommend_tier asks
library::recommend for the tier; the sysctl / meminfo / nvidia-smi /
PowerShell readers and the threshold constants are deleted. NODE_RESERVE_BYTES
is sizeup's constant (7 GiB pin test kept). fleet::role_for maps through
library::Role. Tests: -6 parser tests, +8 library tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Lqmrq4rH9YBGCDmmemAG8H
